## Program Outcome

CEO directives can accumulate durably before implementation and can be added while another
directive is executing, while existing planning order and subordinate cycles remain the only
scheduling and execution authorities.

## M1-DURABLE-CEO-INTAKE — Deliver the local candidate

Status: accepted
Required Endpoint: Work1

Outcome: Make new directive commands capture-only, make exact active matches delegate or resume,
preserve non-preemptive planning order, expose active-first directive state locally and on the
hosted CEO tab, and checkpoint a verified local candidate.

Gates:

- `G1-DURABLE-BATCH-INTAKE` — repeated unmatched CEO commands create separate durable Idea/outcome
  records without starting subordinate implementation.
- `G2-NON-PREEMPTIVE-ORDER` — new directives append through canonical planning order and never
  displace a working subordinate cycle absent an explicit CEO priority change.
- `G3-SUBORDINATE-EXECUTION` — an exact active match delegates or resumes through the existing Plan
  Cycle, PRM, campaign, evidence, and outcome chain without a CEO-side execution queue.
- `G4-CEO-VISIBILITY-RECOVERY` — local and hosted CEO views distinguish queued, working, and
  completed directives; active directives are retained inside a bounded, explicitly truncated
  contract; focused checks, full validation, and checkpoint/rebuild parity pass.

Candidate campaign: `durable-ceo-directive-intake`.

## Authority Boundaries

This roadmap authorizes local source, contract, template, documentation, test, managed artifact,
checkpoint, manifest, and commit changes. It does not authorize deployment, push, release,
production reporting, credential changes, or installed-client synchronization.
